{% comment %}
  Step 4 (shown as "Step 3 of 5") — pick a day and time slot.

  Real backend data: kal-booking-flow.js fetches real per-doctor
  availability on arrival at this step (refreshDayStrip() +
  refreshSlotsForSelectedDate(), both called from goToStep()) and on every
  date/doctor change. The 5 day-strip buttons and 3 Morning/Afternoon/
  Evening slot-grid panels below are markup shells only — their final
  labels/dates/badges/times always come from that JS, synchronously
  overwritten (loading state first, then the real fetch result) before
  the step is ever actually visible, so there's no static placeholder
  content a visitor can see. Only genuinely unavailable slots are ever
  shown at all — see renderSlotPanels()'s own comment for why disabled/
  struck-through slots were dropped entirely rather than just greyed out.
  - Header uses the shared kal-booking-flow-step-header.liquid snippet
    (back/facility badge/close + step progress bar).
  - The doctor summary line is the shared "appointment card" (photo,
    "YOUR CONSULTATION" eyebrow, name, mode + price), same
    .kal-appointment-card* component Patient Details uses — driven by the
    same data-kal-doctor-*-display hooks applySelectedDoctorToCards() in
    kal-booking-flow.js already populates.
  - "Available time" is a Morning/Afternoon/Evening TAB bar (only one
    panel visible at a time). Kept as plain .kal-slot-chip buttons with
    data-kal-slot-start/-end attributes the click handler and
    Confirmation-summary formatting expect.
  - The calendar icon next to "CHOOSE A SLOT" (data-kal-open-calendar)
    opens the calendar modal, enforcing the same date restrictions as the
    real CMS's staff-side SlotPicker.tsx (today bookable, nothing before
    today or beyond today+90 days selectable — see kal-booking-flow.js's
    CALENDAR comment for exact citations), and fetches real availability
    for whichever month is visible (ensureMonthAvailabilityLoaded()).

  Single shared markup, not a __mobile + __desktop split — see the "SHARED
  STEP SHELL" comment in kal-booking-flow.css for why and how the layout
  switches at 750px.

  DESKTOP REDESIGN: same left column + full-width footer as Concern
  Select/Doctor Select now (see kal-booking-flow.css's
  .kal-step-shell--progress-panel section and kal-booking-flow-step-progress.liquid),
  current_step: 3 here — "Health concerns" and "Mode & doctor" both show
  completed, "Date & time" current. Mobile keeps its own "Pick your
  visit" composition untouched below.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-slot-picker kal-step-shell kal-step-shell--progress-panel">

  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info kal-concern-select__info">
    <div class="kal-concern-select__info-scroll">
      <div class="kal-concern-select__info-header">
        <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading kal-concern-select__heading">Consultation Booking</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-concern-select__info-section">
        <p class="kal-concern-select__info-label">Selected Clinic</p>
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-facility-picker', step_number: 3, location_text: 'Indiranagar', extra_class: 'kal-concern-select__info-pill' -%}
      </div>

      {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-progress', current_step: 3 -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-header', back_target: 'doctor-select', step_number: 3, step_total: 5, next_label: 'Personal details' -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Heading moved OUTSIDE .kal-step-shell__scroll (still a sibling
      within .kal-step-shell__panel) per explicit instruction — only the
      heading stays fixed right below the progress bar; the appointment
      card scrolls together with the day-strip/time-slot content below
      it (unlike Patient Details' copy of this same card, which stays
      fixed — explicit instruction to treat this step differently).
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
      <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Choose a date and time</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      {%- assign appointment_photo_url = 'kal-doctor-photo-placeholder.jpg' | asset_url -%}
      {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-appointment-card', photo_url: appointment_photo_url, name: 'Dr. Neethu Jayachandran', price: '&#8377;500' -%}

      <div class="kal-slot-section">
        <div class="kal-slot-section__head">
          <p class="kal-slot-section__label">Choose a Slot</p>
          <button type="button" class="kal-icon-button kal-icon-button--round" data-kal-open-calendar aria-label="Open calendar">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'calendar-month' -%}
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="kal-day-strip">
          {%- comment -%}
            Fully real/dynamic now — kal-booking-flow.js's refreshDayStrip()
            builds one real .kal-day-chip per bookable day (today through
            the same 90-day cap the calendar modal enforces, see
            CALENDAR_MAX_FUTURE_DAYS) and appends them here on arrival at
            this step. Explicit instruction: every bookable date must be
            reachable by scrolling this strip, not just a fixed 5-day
            window — no static placeholder chips to keep in sync with that,
            so this starts empty. .kal-day-strip__track's own CSS already
            handles the horizontal scroll (overflow-x:auto, flex-shrink:0
            chips) — built for exactly this, see that rule's own comment.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="kal-day-strip__track" data-kal-day-strip-track></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Real hold-placement/replace failure (handleSlotContinue() in
        kal-booking-flow.js, on a lost race) — the "that slot was just
        booked" banner. Sits between the day strip and the Morning/
        Afternoon/Evening tabs, same spot at both mobile and desktop (see
        kal-booking-flow.css's min-width:750px override on
        .kal-slot-conflict-banner for the desktop-only margin adjustment) —
        not inline with the footer buttons like a field-validation error.
        This is a standalone amber info banner, not a form error, so it
        gets its own kal-slot-conflict-banner component (see
        kal-booking-flow.css) rather than reusing the shared
        .kal-form-error look that Patient Details' field errors and the
        Confirmation/Therapy Details booking-failure banners still use as-
        is. ONE instance only, unlike those other steps' separate mobile-
        footer + desktop-grid-sibling pair (that split exists so a banner
        meant for the desktop footer row doesn't also render inside the
        mobile panel) — this banner was never in the footer to begin with,
        so there's nothing to duplicate; a second, desktop-positioned copy
        was tried here too and showed both at once at desktop width,
        since the shared .kal-step-shell--progress-panel >
        [data-kal-booking-error] hide/show rule only ever covers DIRECT
        children of the panel, and this one deliberately isn't. Removed.
        data-kal-booking-error/data-kal-booking-error-text are unchanged —
        showBookingError()/clearBookingError() in the JS target every
        element carrying those attributes generically, regardless of which
        visual class wraps them.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="kal-slot-conflict-banner" data-kal-booking-error hidden>
        <span class="kal-slot-conflict-banner__icon">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'info' -%}</span>
        <span data-kal-booking-error-text></span>
      </p>

      <div class="kal-slot-tabs">
        <div class="kal-slot-tabs__bar">
          <button type="button" class="kal-slot-tab kal-slot-tab--active" data-kal-slot-tab="morning">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'period-morning' -%}
            <span class="kal-slot-tab__label">MORNING</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="kal-slot-tab" data-kal-slot-tab="afternoon">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'period-afternoon' -%}
            <span class="kal-slot-tab__label">AFTERNOON</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="kal-slot-tab" data-kal-slot-tab="evening">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'period-evening' -%}
            <span class="kal-slot-tab__label">EVENING</span>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div data-kal-slot-periods>
          <div class="kal-slot-grid" data-kal-slot-panel="morning">
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="09:00:00" data-kal-slot-end="09:45:00">9:00 AM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="09:30:00" data-kal-slot-end="10:15:00">9:30 AM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="09:45:00" data-kal-slot-end="10:30:00">9:45 AM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="10:00:00" data-kal-slot-end="10:45:00">10:00 AM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="10:15:00" data-kal-slot-end="11:00:00">10:15 AM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip kal-slot-chip--active" data-kal-slot-start="10:30:00" data-kal-slot-end="11:15:00">10:30 AM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="11:00:00" data-kal-slot-end="11:45:00">11:00 AM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="11:15:00" data-kal-slot-end="12:00:00">11:15 AM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="11:30:00" data-kal-slot-end="12:15:00">11:30 AM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="11:45:00" data-kal-slot-end="12:30:00">11:45 AM</button>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-slot-grid" data-kal-slot-panel="afternoon" hidden>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="12:00:00" data-kal-slot-end="12:45:00">12:00 PM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="12:30:00" data-kal-slot-end="13:15:00">12:30 PM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="13:00:00" data-kal-slot-end="13:45:00">1:00 PM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="13:30:00" data-kal-slot-end="14:15:00">1:30 PM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="14:00:00" data-kal-slot-end="14:45:00">2:00 PM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="14:30:00" data-kal-slot-end="15:15:00">2:30 PM</button>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-slot-grid" data-kal-slot-panel="evening" hidden>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="16:00:00" data-kal-slot-end="16:45:00">4:00 PM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="16:30:00" data-kal-slot-end="17:15:00">4:30 PM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="17:00:00" data-kal-slot-end="17:45:00">5:00 PM</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-slot-chip" data-kal-slot-start="17:30:00" data-kal-slot-end="18:15:00">5:30 PM</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__footer kal-concern-select__footer kal-concern-select__footer--mobile">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-goto="patient-details" data-kal-slot-continue disabled>
        <span class="kal-button-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span data-kal-continue-label aria-live="polite">Continue</span>
      </button>
    </div>

  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Desktop-only full-width footer bar, same pattern as Concern Select/
    Doctor Select's (see their own liquid comments) — help text + Back
    (to Doctor Select)/Continue split across the shared 300px/1fr grid
    columns. Continue is disabled until a slot is actually picked
    (data-kal-slot-continue, toggled by updateSlotContinueButton() in
    kal-booking-flow.js) — no slot is pre-selected on this step anymore,
    same disabled-until-chosen pattern as Doctor Select's own Continue.
    Clicking it (handleSlotContinue() in the JS) only then places/replaces
    the real hold and navigates on to Patient Details once that succeeds —
    picking a chip itself never holds anything, see that function's own
    comment for why.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-shell__footer kal-concern-select__footer kal-concern-select__footer--desktop">
    <div class="kal-concern-select__footer-help kal-step-entry__help">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--help">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'help-circle' -%}
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__help-text">Need assistance? Call us at +91 804012 3456</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kal-concern-select__footer-actions">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back kal-concern-select__footer-back" data-kal-back="doctor-select" aria-label="Back">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-left' -%}
        <span>Back</span>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-goto="patient-details" data-kal-slot-continue disabled>
        <span class="kal-button-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span data-kal-continue-label aria-live="polite">Continue</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
